{"vid":"fLJWuMvtTrI","source":"fLJWuMvtTrI.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"Being the last line before the"},{"t":1.7,"txt":"medication actually gets into the hands"},{"t":3,"txt":"of patients, that could be make or break"},{"t":5.4,"txt":"for that specific patient."},{"t":9.7,"txt":">> My name is Umberto. I'm a clinical"},{"t":11.2,"txt":"assistant professor at a school of"},{"t":12.3,"txt":"pharmacy. I've been in practice for 23"},{"t":14.3,"txt":"years."},{"t":14.8,"txt":">> I'm Michael. I am a inpatient pharmacist"},{"t":18,"txt":"working [music] with"},{"t":19.7,"txt":"a hospital chain in New Jersey."},{"t":21.6,"txt":">> My name is Sindhu. I am a new grad"},{"t":23.8,"txt":"PharmD, [music] so just graduated in"},{"t":25.6,"txt":"May. Currently, I'm doing post-doctoral"},{"t":28.2,"txt":"training through [music] a fellowship."},{"t":32.4,"txt":">> My day normally starts [music] at the"},{"t":34,"txt":"hospital on average around 7:00. It's"},{"t":37.2,"txt":"first ensuring that the control"},{"t":39.2,"txt":"medications [music]"},{"t":39.9,"txt":"are stocked for the entire hospital."},{"t":41.4,"txt":"Could be a process that takes 30 minutes"},{"t":44,"txt":"to an hour, and it's something where you"},{"t":46.2,"txt":"want to be meticulous. The last thing"},{"t":47.8,"txt":"you want is like the DEA knocking at"},{"t":49.8,"txt":"your door saying like, \"Then your"},{"t":51.6,"txt":"numbers are off.\""},{"t":52.5,"txt":">> One day a week I'm giving a lecture on"},{"t":55.1,"txt":"campus. Maybe half day spent at the"},{"t":57.4,"txt":"clinic. While I'm at the clinic, I'm"},{"t":59.3,"txt":"reviewing patient charts, touching base"},{"t":61.5,"txt":"with the provider, seeing if they need"},{"t":63,"txt":"anything, working with insurance"},{"t":65.2,"txt":"companies, with pharmacies, taking"},{"t":67.8,"txt":"calls, sending authorizations to get the"},{"t":70.9,"txt":"patient's medications approved."},{"t":72.6,"txt":">> During my actual 9:00 to 5:00, right now"},{"t":74.6,"txt":"I'm focused on medical content and"},{"t":76.1,"txt":"training. So, providing training for new"},{"t":79.6,"txt":"data that's coming out from clinical"},{"t":81.2,"txt":"trials to medical science liaisons and"},{"t":84.3,"txt":"other members of the healthcare"},{"t":85.3,"txt":"community so they we can raise awareness"},{"t":88,"txt":"of the different treatment options that"},{"t":89.7,"txt":"[music] are out there."},{"t":92.2,"txt":">> Uh like what's the biggest obstacle a"},{"t":93.9,"txt":"lot of time is interpersonal skills. One"},{"t":95.8,"txt":"of the hardest things to do where a lot"},{"t":97.9,"txt":"of times it's we have to meet the"},{"t":99.5,"txt":"patients in in the arenas they are, but"},{"t":101.4,"txt":"also co-workers, employees."},{"t":104.2,"txt":">> I think also like growth mindset because"},{"t":107.8,"txt":"the field is changing, and if you don't"},{"t":110.9,"txt":"change with the field, you're going to"},{"t":112.5,"txt":"be left behind."},{"t":113.5,"txt":">> With any healthcare profession, there's"},{"t":114.8,"txt":"continuing education. You have to be"},{"t":116.5,"txt":"really willing to keep on learning and"},{"t":118.4,"txt":"keep on being adaptable to, you know,"},{"t":120.3,"txt":"new medications that are coming out. As"},{"t":121.8,"txt":"a new grad pharmacist, there is a lot"},{"t":123.2,"txt":"more emphasis on technology and, you"},{"t":125.2,"txt":"know, being able to integrate that into"},{"t":127.5,"txt":"our work. And also being"},{"t":128.9,"txt":"detail-oriented, especially with"},{"t":130.5,"txt":"medications, being the last line before"},{"t":132.7,"txt":"the medication actually gets into the"},{"t":133.9,"txt":"hands of patients, that could be make or"},{"t":136.4,"txt":"break for that specific patient. And I"},{"t":138,"txt":"think having that perspective, you're"},{"t":139.4,"txt":"impacting people at the end of the day,"},{"t":141.1,"txt":"is really important."},{"t":142.4,"txt":">> Whatever the skill set, put a language"},{"t":143.8,"txt":"in your back pocket. If you want a"},{"t":145,"txt":"patient to tell you anything, just drop"},{"t":147.2,"txt":"like a welcome in their home language,"},{"t":149,"txt":"they'll tell you everything."},{"t":150.4,"txt":">> Ensure that it's not just about a"},{"t":153.3,"txt":"disease state and a medication, that you"},{"t":156.2,"txt":"you you [music] see past that and you"},{"t":157.6,"txt":"see how that's really impacting the"},{"t":159.2,"txt":"person."},{"t":163.3,"txt":">> Pharmacy programs [music]"},{"t":164.8,"txt":"are usually post-undergrad or graduate"},{"t":167.8,"txt":"level. There are some that are hybrid"},{"t":169.9,"txt":"that could be a accelerated undergrad"},{"t":172.9,"txt":"graduate combined."},{"t":174.3,"txt":">> So, you have different programs that are"},{"t":175.9,"txt":"popping up that are dual degrees. So,"},{"t":178.5,"txt":"you just have to make sure you do your"},{"t":179.8,"txt":"research and see what options are out"},{"t":182.1,"txt":"there."},{"t":182.5,"txt":">> You are done with your PharmD degree,"},{"t":184.8,"txt":"you apply to take two licensure exams,"},{"t":188,"txt":"right? So, your law exam for the"},{"t":190.1,"txt":"specific state you want to practice in"},{"t":191.7,"txt":"and then the NAPLEX. And you are"},{"t":193.8,"txt":"required to pass both of those after a"},{"t":195.6,"txt":"certain amount of practice hours,"},{"t":197.5,"txt":"usually in your fourth year of pharmacy"},{"t":198.7,"txt":"school, in order to become a registered"},{"t":200.5,"txt":"pharmacist and be able to work in"},{"t":202.3,"txt":"patient care settings."},{"t":206.6,"txt":">> Your interview process [music] starts"},{"t":208.3,"txt":"the moment you start your clinical"},{"t":209.6,"txt":"experience. So, every time you go into a"},{"t":211.1,"txt":"hospital, a retail chain, a big pharma"},{"t":213.8,"txt":"company, you're actively interviewing."},{"t":216.4,"txt":">> Treating interviews as conversations is"},{"t":218.6,"txt":"really important because I know when I"},{"t":220.5,"txt":"first started interviewing for"},{"t":221.9,"txt":"internships, I was very very robotic."},{"t":224.4,"txt":"And I think that is a really acquired"},{"t":225.8,"txt":"skill that comes with a lot of practice."},{"t":227.5,"txt":"Like, we should be relying on our"},{"t":228.5,"txt":"mentors, like our preceptors, to be"},{"t":229.8,"txt":"like, \"Okay, do you mind just like"},{"t":231.3,"txt":"running through how I can explain my"},{"t":233.8,"txt":"experiences with you so you can give me"},{"t":236.1,"txt":"feedback and I can, you know, actually"},{"t":238,"txt":"showcase the impact I've made."},{"t":239.4,"txt":">> Your mentors are going to give you the"},{"t":241,"txt":"best critique. They're probably going to"},{"t":242.3,"txt":"shred you and you're probably going to"},{"t":244.2,"txt":"feel like the worst of the worst, but"},{"t":246.4,"txt":"what better place for it to happen when"},{"t":248.5,"txt":"it's a test run, it's not the actual"},{"t":250.3,"txt":"thing. Your mentors are always going to"},{"t":252.3,"txt":"help you create the CV, talk about the"},{"t":254.2,"txt":"job that you [music] want, and just you"},{"t":255.7,"txt":"is their your soundboard."},{"t":259.2,"txt":">> Usually pharmacy residents and fellows"},{"t":261.1,"txt":"make [music] a little less and then"},{"t":262.6,"txt":"after you're done with your"},{"t":264.8,"txt":"post-doctoral training, at least for"},{"t":266.1,"txt":"fellowship, it it can really vary."},{"t":268,"txt":">> As a clinical specialist, you'll get"},{"t":270,"txt":"paid more as a clinical specialist"},{"t":271.5,"txt":"anything from 110 to 160, 170,000"},{"t":275.8,"txt":"depending on the specialty. As a faculty"},{"t":277.9,"txt":"member, you're you're getting paid less."},{"t":279.7,"txt":">> And inpatient, I think it's roughly"},{"t":281.2,"txt":"around the same. You're looking at"},{"t":282.7,"txt":"anywhere between 120 to about like 150,"},{"t":287.9,"txt":"160 and it's normally based on like the"},{"t":290.2,"txt":"amount of years worked and also the"},{"t":291.9,"txt":"chain that you're with."},{"t":292.9,"txt":">> A lot of clinical pharmacists end up"},{"t":294.9,"txt":"going into industry and working within"},{"t":298,"txt":"clinical trials, medical affairs, drug"},{"t":301,"txt":"info, you know, marketing even. So, I I"},{"t":303.9,"txt":"know many examples of folks that"},{"t":306,"txt":"hopefully our roles will continue to"},{"t":308.5,"txt":"[music] allow for for some of that"},{"t":310.7,"txt":"growth."},{"t":315.2,"txt":">> We [music] cover every single disease"},{"t":317.6,"txt":"that you can think of. So, at any point"},{"t":319.4,"txt":"in time the phone rings, you pick it up"},{"t":321.4,"txt":"and you have to speak to neuro, heart,"},{"t":324.6,"txt":"kidney, lung, infectious disease, like"},{"t":327.2,"txt":"and it's like, uh, go. I feel like I"},{"t":329.2,"txt":"have the baddest swagger around at"},{"t":331.2,"txt":"times."},{"t":331.9,"txt":">> As someone who like loves research and"},{"t":333.7,"txt":"love science, being able to work really"},{"t":335.6,"txt":"closely with data really excites me on"},{"t":337.6,"txt":"my day-to-day basis. I feel like I'm not"},{"t":339.2,"txt":"doing the same thing over and over. I"},{"t":341,"txt":"feel like every week and every day looks"},{"t":342.4,"txt":"really different for me."},{"t":343.4,"txt":">> Pharmacy is an evolving field that you"},{"t":346.8,"txt":"can make [music] what you want it to."},{"t":348.9,"txt":"So, take the leap. Check out more job"},{"t":351.6,"txt":"insights right here on Indeed's channel."}],"words":[{"t":0,"w":"Being"},{"t":0.2,"w":"the"},{"t":0.32,"w":"last"},{"t":0.64,"w":"line"},{"t":1,"w":"before"},{"t":1.56,"w":"the"},{"t":1.68,"w":"medication"},{"t":2.12,"w":"actually"},{"t":2.36,"w":"gets"},{"t":2.56,"w":"into"},{"t":2.68,"w":"the"},{"t":2.8,"w":"hands"},{"t":3,"w":"of"},{"t":3.08,"w":"patients,"},{"t":3.